On 12 May 2006, Eva Myers wrote:
> pendell@hotmail.com writes:
>
> > Game-opening break:  Early wand of enlightenment allows me to identify
> > an early ring of regeneration.  This regen ring kept me alive in many
> > dangerous situations, including the endgame.
>
> You didn't need the wand of enlightenment.  Just wear any unidentified
> noncursed ring for a few turns when injured and see whether you heal
> faster.
> Eva.

More specifically, you wear the ring for two game turns while injured.
If you gain HP on -both- turns, you are regenerating, otherwise you are
not.

However, "one game turn" doesn't always mean one move for the player --
burdening and/or speed can interfere.  To avoid confusion, ensure you are
unburdened, turn the "time" option on ("O" command, or in your
.nethackrc), and do not count "turns" where the turncount on your
statusline does not increase.

BTW, wearing nonidentified rings can sometimes be very bad even for a few
turns, even if they are uncursed.  It's best to price-ID first, since the
two main threats are in a different price class than regeneration.

